      "created_at": "2018-08-24T17:52:18.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>About August 6th the Oblivaeon shipping got delivered to Argentina Customs. Unfortunately it's been stuck there and will need to be sent back to origin because they declared the cost of the shipping as U$S 1 (for a box of over 2 kg) which doesn't meet the standard criteria (would need to register as an importer and get a customs dispatcher to handle the red tape to fix it) and can't be introduced into the country.<br><br>Had it been properly declared (about U$S 60 or 100 with shipping included) there would have been no issues, I would have paid some taxes and receivied it in my home. The real kicker is that it takes about 8 months to ship it back to origin (for free). But would need to get the shipper company to then send it again properly declared...</p><p>Oh well...</p>",
